※ pl4g-test: compile=fail
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4548 LANG_NARROW_NOT_AN_INTEGER
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4559 LANG_GENERIC_ASKED_HERE

※ `std.string.parse_int` reads a whole number, of whichever whole-number type
※ it is handed; a floating-point one is `parse_f64`'s, whose grammar has a point
※ and an exponent.  Handed `⌜f64⌝`, the narrowing it ends with is refused for
※ that type, with a note at the call that asked for it -- the refusal of every
※ narrowing to a type that is not a whole number.

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    match std.string.parse_int(⎕bytes("10"), ⌜f64⌝):
        std.string.Parsed(f64)(_):
            0u6
        ⊥:
            1u6
